       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 9,600 mg/day it's three times the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that justifies it. The likely harms are serious: GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS toxicity. A dose like this is an overdose, whatever the patient's kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than these give, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a standard dose.\n\nIf you think there's a real reason for a dose above the maximum, please discuss it with pharmacy first. I can add a note to a different order asking for that review."
      }
